We find the modular inverse of 27 modulo 125 using the Extended Euclidean Algorithm. The inverse of 27 modulo 125 is 93, since $27 \cdot 93 \equiv 1 \pmod{125}$. Multiplying both sides of $27k \equiv 3 \pmod{125}$ by 93 gives:  
$$
k \equiv 3 \cdot 93 \pmod{125} \Rightarrow k \equiv 279 \pmod{125} \Rightarrow k \equiv 34 \pmod{125}
$$  
Thus, $k = 125m + 34$ for some integer $m$, and $x = 27k + 1 = 27(125m + 34) + 1 = 3375m + 919$. Therefore, $x \equiv 919 \pmod{3375}$.  

Now we solve the system:  
$$
\begin{align*}
x &\equiv 919 \pmod{3375} \\
x &\equiv 18 \pmod{343}
\end{align*}
$$

